    "result": "## Summary\n\nI've successfully fixed the bug where `frai gate init --ci` was not creating the GitHub Actions workflow file. \n\n**The Problem:**\nThe `--ci` flag was being consumed by the main `frai` command's option parser instead of being passed through to the `frai-gate` CLI. Commander.js was parsing the flag at the top level and not including it in the arguments passed to the `gate` subcommand handler.\n\n**The Solution:**\nModified `/packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` to use `process.argv` directly to capture all arguments after the 'gate' command, including options. This ensures that all flags and arguments are properly forwarded to the frai-gate CLI.\n\n**Changes Made:**\n- Extracted arguments from `process.argv` using `process.argv.indexOf('gate')` to find where the gate command starts\n- Passed all arguments after 'gate' to the frai-gate process via `spawnSync`\n\n**Verification:**\n- Rebuilt the package with `pnpm --filter frai build`\n- Tested from an empty directory: `node <repo>/packages/frai-cli/dist/index.js gate init --ci`\n- Both `FRAI-SPEC.md` and `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml` are now created successfully",
